1. DEFINITIONS

1.1 "Repository" means the source code repository containing this License.

1.2 "Repository Materials" means all files, folders, and content in the
Repository.

1.3 "Schema Materials" means the specification and registry assets in the
Repository that define or describe a general-purpose document/schema/registry
format, including (without limitation): (a) naming conventions, folder
structures, allowed file types, and formatting rules; (b) schema definitions
(YAML/JSON/etc.), validation rules, registries, and schema tooling; and (c)
examples that exist solely to demonstrate the schema format.

1.4 "Governance Use" means using Schema Materials to create, operate,
administer, execute, or document a governance system or governance process for
any DAO, collective, foundation, protocol governance body, token governance, or
similar arrangement, including (without limitation): proposals, resolutions,
votes, treasury actions, elections, charters, committees/subcommittees, SOPs,
and any instrument intended to be adopted, relied on, or represented as a
governance instrument.

1.5 "Non-Governance Use" means any use of Schema Materials that is not
Governance Use.

1.6 "Governance Materials" means any templates, documents, specifications,
forms, packs, policies, procedures, or other materials in the Repository that
are specific to Solomon DAO governance or designed primarily for Governance Use,
including without limitation: proposals, operational packs, SOPs, charters,
operating agreements, bylaws, resolutions, notices, governance registries, and
governance-specific templates or forms, whether included in the Repository
intentionally or inadvertently.

1.7 "MetaDAO Cohort" means an entity designated as a cohort under the MetaDAO
governance system (as determined by MetaDAO governance records).

1.8 "Governance Repository" means the Solomon DAO public governance repository
(as designated by the Solomon DAO governance system from time to time).

1.9 "Governance License" means the license titled "SOLOMON DAO LLC PUBLIC
GOVERNANCE REPOSITORY LICENSE" as published in the Governance Repository.

1.10 "Implementation" means any deployment, system, product, service, issuer,
custody setup, market, or other operational arrangement that uses Protocol IP.

